From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - fail a CCM decryption whose ICV does not match

On BCM6755, SPU-M does not flag a CCM ICV mismatch with the error flag
and SPU_STATUS_INVALID_ICV, as it does for GCM (status 0xc0020100).
It sets bit 24 of the status word instead and nothing else, so the
driver accepts the bad tag:

  alg: aead: ccm-aes-iproc decryption unexpectedly succeeded on test
  vector 16; expected_error=-EBADMSG, cfg="in-place (one sglist)"
  alg: aead: ccm-aes-esp-iproc decryption unexpectedly succeeded on
  test vector "random: alen=16 plen=15 authsize=16 klen=35 novrfy=1";
  expected_error=-EBADMSG or -22, ...

In a self-test run, the two bad-tag CCM decryptions returned status
0x01000000, and the 3709 CCM and 3733 GCM decryptions with a good tag
returned 0. A tamper test then decrypted 34 CCM messages for each ICV
size SPU-M handles (8, 12 and 16 bytes): once unmodified, then with
one bit flipped in each ICV byte, in the ciphertext and in the
associated data. All 1398 modified messages returned exactly
0x01000000, and all unmodified ones returned 0. The vendor SPU headers
do not name this bit.

Report a status with bit 24 set as an ICV mismatch.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/spu.c  | 2 ++
 drivers/crypto/bcm/spum.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/spu.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/spu.c
@@ -1112,6 +1112,8 @@ int spum_status_process(u8 *statp)
 
 	status = __be32_to_cpu(*(__be32 *)statp);
 	flow_log("SPU response STATUS %#08x\n", status);
+	if (status & SPU_STATUS_CCM_INVALID_ICV)
+		return SPU_INVALID_ICV;
 	if (status & SPU_STATUS_ERROR_FLAG) {
 		pr_err("%s() Warning: Error result from SPU: %#08x\n",
 		       __func__, status);
--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/spum.h
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/spum.h
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #define SPU_STATUS_MASK                 0x0000FF00
 #define SPU_STATUS_SUCCESS              0x00000000
 #define SPU_STATUS_INVALID_ICV          0x00000100
+#define SPU_STATUS_CCM_INVALID_ICV      0x01000000
 
 #define SPU_STATUS_ERROR_FLAG           0x00020000
 
